      "scene_type": "gritwerk_paper",
      "duration_hint": 21,
      "spoken": "In the first study, eighty-seven students studied online for one day. Some took breaks when they felt like it, others followed a fixed rhythm, such as twenty-four minutes of study and six minutes of break. With the fixed rhythm, they reported less fatigue and better concentration. They got the same amount done.",
